     D2's bench reading turns it into a margin); the VBAT stages' EN/UVLO pins are driven by logic (the slot, device, PA, HF, PoE and PD stages)
     and the heater buck's divider starts it at about 7.3 V, so no VSYS divider sets a line above VSYS_MIN; A-14's assumed 10.0 V converter floor
     is under it too (NETLIST, INFERRED)
   the kit's declared steps (r4a's loop design, INFERRED there; efficiencies from gen_sch_a.py; the mat from hc2) at VSYS, and whether R-c's envelope
     admits each on top of P1's plan 19.57 W at the widest source (36 V, 84.55 W) (INFERRED):
     S2 slot rail (+5V_S2, a 5G burst)            3 A at 5.09 V over 0.9 (ASSUMPTION (+5V_DEV's declared 0.90)): 16.97 W at VSYS; admitted in S4; the fallback holds it 3.187 ms (INFERRED)
     SD device rail (+5V_DEV)                     3 A at 5.09 V over 0.9 (NETLIST): 16.97 W at VSYS; admitted in S4; the fallback holds it 3.187 ms (INFERRED)
     PA rail (+13V8_PA, a 30 W carrier keyed)     5.4 A at 13.76 V over 0.93 (NETLIST): 79.9 W at VSYS; not admitted in S4 (R-c holds it); the fallback holds it 0.677 ms (INFERRED)
     HF rail (+12V_HF)                            2 A at 12 V over 0.93 (NETLIST): 25.81 W at VSYS; admitted in S4; the fallback holds it 2.095 ms (INFERRED)
     PoE rail (+54V_POE)                          0.6 A at 54 V over 0.88 (NETLIST): 36.82 W at VSYS; admitted in S4; the fallback holds it 1.469 ms (INFERRED)
     USB-C PD outlet at 15 V (PD_VPWR)            3 A at 15 V over 0.93 (NETLIST): 48.39 W at VSYS; admitted in S4; the fallback holds it 1.117 ms (INFERRED)
     the pack heater mat, regulated (on)          8.5 W (RECORD): 8.5 W at VSYS; admitted in S4; the fallback holds it 6.361 ms (INFERRED)
   the worst admitted step: USB-C PD outlet at 15 V (PD_VPWR), 48.39 W, 3.934 A at the floor (INFERRED)
   THE FALLBACK (SESSION; a register row, E11-24, never applied):
     a direct can on VSYS: one Panasonic EEHZK1V181P (180 uF 35 V, F size 8.0 x 10.2 mm, ESR 27 mOhm; LCSC C242139); and a hold-up bank: 4 x EEHZK1E471P
     (470 uF 25 V, G size 10.0 x 10.2 mm, ESR 20 mOhm; C242138), charged from VSYS through R_CH 330 Ohm (Yageo RC2512FK-07330RL, 1 W at 70 C, C137025) and
     discharging into VSYS through D_H, a Diodes B540C-13-F (40 V, 5 A, VF at most 0.55 V at 5 A and 25 C; C72264) (MAKER, CATALOGUE)
   the capacitance's derating (Panasonic ZK sheet): +-20 % tolerance, endurance within +-30 %, no DC-bias dependence (an aluminium hybrid polymer part, its class),
     the low-temperature change not printed ("as small as polymer type"): 0.9 at -20 C (ASSUMPTION); so 0.504 of nominal at the stacked worst (MAKER, ASSUMPTION)
   the bank: 947.5 uF effective; it sits at 16.561 V (the leakage, 0.01 CV uA a can, across R_CH) and gives into VSYS down to 12.95 V (VSYS_MIN plus D_H's
     0.65 V: its 25 C maximum plus 0.1 V at -20 C, ASSUMPTION): 48.26 mJ net of the diode; the direct can 90.72 uF effective from 16.716 to 12.3 V: 5.81 mJ;
     54.07 mJ in all, the MLCCs not counted (N4) (INFERRED)
   against the worst admitted step: 1.117 ms of hold, over the 1 ms assumed (MEETS, CONDITIONAL on T_RESP); the least cans for a hold of: 0.25 ms 1, 0.5 ms 2, 1 ms 4, 2 ms 8, 5 ms 20 (INFERRED)
   size: four G cans (10.3 mm square lands, 10.5 mm tall at most), one F can, an SMC diode and a 2512: about 5.5 cm2 of board A (INFERRED)
   placement: board A, on VBAT (the charger's VSYS); board P is behind the pack's FETs, which are open in S4, so it cannot hold VSYS there (NETLIST, INFERRED);
     the height and the zone are Layer 9's (L4-E8 placed six G cans on board A's VBUS20, so the class fits the board) (INFERRED)
   inrush, the entry and F1: the bank charges through R_CH at 51.2 mA at most, 0.864 W at most against the resistor's 1 W at 70 C (the inside air 62.1 C), with
     a time constant of 0.744 s and 0.322 J per full charge; the direct can charges with VSYS under the charger's own start (0.5 A until 1.6 V, 3 min allowed,
     9.3.21.8; 1.93 ms to 1.6 V at that current); the entry's start ends before U34 releases the front end (79 ms at least), so neither the entry's
     inrush nor F1's I2t changes (MEETS, INFERRED)
   inrush from the pack (S1 from cold, VSYS discharged, the discharge FET switching at once): the direct can and the MLCCs (352.2 uF nominal, 603.4 uF at
     most) through the pack's least loop 69.17 mOhm (four cells at 35 mOhm over three, and pwr_budget's distribution): 242.9 A peak, over the image's ASCD
     55.6 A for 61.5 us against its 183 us delay (MEETS, INFERRED); the bank behind R_CH adds 51.2 mA, so it cannot trip ASCD (INFERRED)
   what it does not do (INFERRED):
     a step beyond the source's headroom is a deficit, not a transient: at a 9.00 V plug the slot rail's step on P1's plan leaves 7.45 W short, which the
       fallback only delays by 7.26 ms; R-c's measured headroom must therefore count the largest uncontrolled step of the loads P1 keeps (E11-06 measures P1's peaks)
     in S2 (a warm CUV) VSYS is the stack plus Q2's diode, 10 to 11 V, at A-14's assumed 10.0 V floor: no droop is left to hold, so S2 still rests on
       the charger's response (D2 for S2) and on the converters' real minimum inputs (E11-08)
     it settles neither D1 (the steady mode) nor D3 (the inhibited mode): no capacitance answers what the converter regulates

11. WHAT CHANGES FOR U-04'S CLASSIFICATION (INFERRED)
   made independent of TI by the fallback: D2 for every admitted step in S4 within the bank's 1.117 ms (with D2's bench margin), and D5 (VSYS's
     effective capacitance) by the direct can (INFERRED)
   still depending on TI: D1 (S4 at all), D3 (REQ-077's hold and R-a's S2), D4 (low consequence), D6 (the image's 0-V charging), D7 and D8 (R-b's
     cases (iii) and (ii)); and on the entry's makers: D9 and D10
   negative answers with a remedy inside arrangement (A): D4, D5, D6, D7, D8, D9, D10; with none: D1 and D3, whose negative answers return (B)
   so U-04 STAYS AN ARCHITECTURE-LEVEL CHOICE: the fallback narrows the architecture's dependence on TI from four statements (D1, D2, D3, D5) to two
     (D1, D3), but those two decide whether arrangement (A) can run on a source with no usable pack and hold a charge while carried, and no part,
     rule or capacitance inside (A) answers them; one bench sample can show the mode on that silicon revision, not a production-wide behaviour

12. THE U-04 QUESTION FOR THE CONSOLIDATION: TI'S BQ25730 AGAINST BOARD A'S CIRCUIT (2 October 2026)
   the owner's instructions of 2 October 2026: 11:25, compare at most three credible approaches, prefer adequate margin and fewer interacting
     controls, quantify power, heat, space, cost and endurance, select the best-supported route, retain the work done unless the change affects it;
     12:00, the charger that supports the battery-present, battery-absent and charging-inhibited modes, the BQ25730 against TI's sheet and
     board A's circuit: interfaces, settings, startup, protection and the affected budgets (REQUIREMENT, the owner's)
   the sheet: TI BQ25730, SLUSE65A (February 2021, revised January 2024), 111 pages, held back under TI's terms (fetch_held_back.py); p.1: "Power path
     control through battery MOSFET implementing independent system voltage instant-on with no battery or depleted battery" (MAKER)
   12a. THE PINS AGAINST U3'S NETLIST (gen_sch_a.py, U3 C2871872)
     the two pin tables (SLUSE66A and SLUSE65A, pp.5 to 7) name 31 of 32 pins alike; the one difference: pin 21, NC on the BQ25731 ("must be
       floating", U3 draws it NC) and BATDRV on the BQ25730, the P-channel BATFET's gate drive, "shorted to VSYS to turn off ... 10 V below VSYS
       to fully turn on" (p.5) (MAKER, NETLIST)
     added: Q39, a P-channel FET, source on VBAT (pin 22, VSYS), drain on a new node CH_BATQ, gate on CH_BATDRV (pin 21); R17 (the 5 mOhm RSR)
       moves to CH_BATQ to CELL_FUSED and R149 (SRP's 10 Ohm) to CH_BATQ, as TI's Figure 9-1 draws the BATFET between VSYS and RSR (SESSION)
     same pin, new function: VSYS (22) becomes a regulated output, "maximum limit ... ChargeVoltage register plus 150 mV and regulation minimum
       limit ... VSYS_MIN register" (p.7); SRP (20) reads the BATFET's side of RSR; every other pin keeps its net and function (MAKER, NETLIST)
     CELL_BATPRESZ (18) keeps the 4S strap (75.14 percent of VDDA): pulled low it would load VSYS_MIN 3.6 V, SYSOVP 25 V and ChargeVoltage 4.2 V
       (p.29), so battery presence is never wired to it (SESSION, MAKER)
   12b. THE SETTINGS L4-E4 TO L4-E8 DRAFTED, SHEET AGAINST SHEET (the electrical tables of SLUSE66A 8.5 and SLUSE65A 7.5, read row by row)
     98 of the BQ25731's 107 row blocks are identical in the BQ25730's table; the rows the drafted settings rest on are among them (MAKER, INFERRED):
       VBAT_REG_ACC, VIREG_CHG_RNG, IIIN_DPM_REG_ACC, VIREG_DPM_RNG_ILIM, IIIN_DPM_REG_ACC_ILIM, VDPM_REG_ACC, VREGN_REG, VVBUSOV_RISE, VVBUSOV_FALL, VACOC_FLOOR
       VACOC_CEILING, VSYSOVP_RISE, VSYSOVP_FALL, VBATOVP_RISE, VBATOVP_FALL, VOCP_lim_ACX, VOCP_lim_Q2, VOCP_lim_SYSSHRT_ACX, VOCP_lim_SYSSHRT_Q2, TSHUT_RISE
       VHIZ_, VCELL_4S, VCELL_BATPRESZ_FALL, IDCHG_TH1, IDCHG_TH2, VPSYS_ACC, VIADPT_ACC, IIBAT_CHG_ACC, VVBUS_CONVEN, VVBAT_UVLOZ; ChargeCurrent's accuracy -12% / 13.5% / -18% / 21.5%, the 400 kHz row and REGN's limit the same (MAKER)
     rows whose numbers differ: VSYS_UVLOZ 1.5/1.7/1.85 V to 2.3/2.5/2.65 V and VSYS_UVLO 1.4/1.6/1.75 V to 2.2/2.4/2.55 V (changed); IDCHG_TH2's typical 24.567 A reprinted 24.576 A;
