14. THE SELECTION, THE DRAFT AND U-04'S CLASS
   SELECTED (SESSION): (B1), TI's BQ25730 in U3's land with Q39 (the fix round, 15c: Q39 and Q40, two BUK6Y10-30P; 15a: board E on VSYS).
     Why: it is the only option whose maker prints a bound on VSYS in all three modes
     (12c), removing D1, D3 and D4 and bounding D7 inside 0 to 85 C, where (A) leaves D1 and D3 to TI and holds D2 with compensating parts on an
     assumed 1 ms; every setting L4-E4 to L4-E8 drafted rests on rows the two sheets print alike (12b); it costs less and removes the bank; its
     costs are named and bounded: Q39's thermal bar (E11-29), the docking pulse (E11-30), 0.221 % of the pack's output at PS-IDLE-SPEC, and
     the BQ25730's stock (E11-32). No protected line changes and no money beyond parts (reserved.json names no schematic part) (SESSION)
   the draft: apply_gen_sch_a_charger.py (release-guarded, never applied here): U3 BQ25730RSNR (C5219071), pin 21 CH_BATDRV, Q39 AONS21357 (C404364) between
     VBAT and CH_BATQ, R17 and R149 moved to CH_BATQ, C236 EEHZK1V181P (C242139) on VBAT, CH_BATQ declared a segment of the pack path (SESSION)
   what it changes downstream: E11-27 to E11-32 added; E11-24 withdrawn and E11-05 not needed once E11-27 is applied; E11-22's case (iii) bounded
     inside 0 to 85 C; Q-TI-11's D1 and Q-TI-3's addendum fall away (D2's question stays); R-a's S4 exception withdrawn; section 3 unchanged (INFERRED)
   U-04's claims still open with (B1): D2 (S2 and S4 load steps against the 2.054 V margin: bench E11-31, fallback R-c's step rule); Q39's thermal
     bar (E11-29) and docking pulse (E11-30); D6, D8 (R-b's case (ii)); REQ-015 at 9.00 V at the plug as section 3g (E11-06, E11-09, E11-23); and
     on board E D9 and D10 (INFERRED)
   U-04 BY THE OWNER'S EXIT DEFINITION: A DOWNSTREAM QUALIFICATION TEST WITH BOUNDED EVIDENCE AND A WORKABLE FALLBACK, once E11-27 is applied:
     the three modes rest on the maker's printed rows; each open claim has a test or analysis that bounds it and a fallback that needs no new
     architecture (R-c's step rule; OCD1 set to the installed path; a slower DSG turn-on on board P). On the drawn board (A) it stays the
     architecture-level choice of section 11 (INFERRED)

15. THE FIX ROUND FOR THE CONSOLIDATION REVIEW (cx36, read NOT YET on set 27's 8fbb68b6: its B1, B2 and the charger minors)
   15a. B1: BOARD E'S AUXILIARY DOMAIN ON A SOURCE-CAPABLE FEED
     as drawn (NETLIST): U12 (the AP63205, its VIN and EN), C31 and both mixer fans (J_FAN1, J_FAN2, D7, D8) sit on CELL_F, the pack node
       before board A's R17 and the battery FET; CELL_F declares them at 1 A (U12 0.8, fans 0.1 and 0.1); the counterexample holds: with
       the charge inhibited the battery FET is off (p.38) and they still drain the pack, and with the pack absent nothing feeds them (NETLIST, MAKER)
     the feed (SESSION): from VSYS alone, over the dock: board A's J_DOCK pin 1 from GND to VBAT (VSYS), board E's J_BLK pin 1 to a new net
       VSYS_E, and U12's VIN and EN, C31, the fans' supply pins and D7 and D8 on VSYS_E; CELL_F keeps the pack path to board A, D3, C1 and
       the pack monitor (R42 and R43). Why VSYS and no OR: VSYS exists whenever the pack or a source does (the battery FET on with the
       battery alone, p.27, and its body diode under any fault of the drive), and a diode or ideal-diode OR with CELL_F would take the pack
       whenever VSYS sits under it, which the +-2 % row allows in the held state (INFERRED)
     the contact: one 813 on pin 1, 1 A declared, 28.6 % of its 3.5 A, 4.9 K by w3de's assumed I2 rise; the seven 813 ground contacts left carry,
       at the 32.1 A coincidence with every Mill-Max pin at 20 mOhm (w3de's model, pinned):
       8 x 813 ground: 2.092 A each, 59.8 % of 3.5 A, 72.4 C at the 51 C air and 86.4 C at the margin's 65 C (INFERRED, w3de's ASSUMPTIONS)
       8 x 813 ground, one open: 2.238 A each, 63.9 % of 3.5 A, 75.5 C at the 51 C air and 89.5 C at the margin's 65 C (INFERRED, w3de's ASSUMPTIONS)
       7 x 813 ground: 2.238 A each, 63.9 % of 3.5 A, 75.5 C at the 51 C air and 89.5 C at the margin's 65 C (INFERRED, w3de's ASSUMPTIONS)
       7 x 813 ground, one open: 2.406 A each, 68.7 % of 3.5 A, 79.3 C at the 51 C air and 93.3 C at the margin's 65 C (INFERRED, w3de's ASSUMPTIONS)
       so taking one ground contact moves W3DE-DOCK-R1's residual by one contact's step and keeps the 51 C envelope under 85 C with one open;
       a second supply contact would leave six, 84.1 C with one open at 51 C: one contact is taken (SESSION); losing it unpowers board E's
       controller, which board A reads on HOT-R1 as the detector lost (IF-AE-DOCK hot_r1), a detected state (INFERRED)
     VSYS_E's range: the supplement floor 9.688 V to 17.375 V (15d); the AP63205 takes 3.8 to 32 V (Diodes DS41326 p.1); the fans, rated as 12 V class
       on CELL_F's 16.884 V, now see up to 17.375 V: their maximum supply voltage is owed (E11-35) (MAKER, INFERRED)
     the held state (the charge inhibited, an adequate source, the pack present): the battery FET off with no charging or supplement current
       (p.38); board E on VSYS_E from the source; what the pack still feeds, by element (MAKER, NETLIST, INFERRED):
       the pack monitor R42 + R43 (122 kOhm at -1 %): 0.1398 mA at 16.884 V, intended (the controller's own pack reading)
       D3, SMCJ18A: IR at most 1 uA at 18 V and 25 C (Littelfuse SMC series, held); its hot leakage is not printed
       the battery FETs' body diodes: VSYSMAX_ACC's -2 % lets VSYS sit up to 0.191 V under the pack at 16.884 V, a forward bias at which the sheets
       print no current (VSD only at 80 A): not bounded on held evidence; and the charger's SRN pin, whose leakage row prints a mismatch only
     so no kit load is fed from the pack while the source carries it; the bounded drains total 0.1408 mA, and the bench reads the held pack
       current at most 1 mA (E11-31's acceptance; board E's aux drew about 0.5 to 1.5 W from the pack before) (SESSION, CONDITIONAL)
     the source-only sequence (the pack absent or both its FETs open): the source and the entry (3c); the front end to VBUS20; U3's POR (p.27),
       ChargeCurrent 0 A; the converter up; VSYS through VSYS_UVP's start (15b) to VSYS_MIN; board A's always-on and board E's U12 on VSYS_E;
       E's controller up and driving HOT-R1; firmware: EN_OOA 0, IIN_HOST 4.70 A, CHRG_INHIBIT from the hold flag (INFERRED, MAKER)
     the held sequence: the flag set writes CHRG_INHIBIT 1; the battery FET turns off as the charge stops (p.38); VSYS moves to VSRN + 150 mV;
       nothing on either board moves; the flag cleared writes 0 and ChargeCurrent by R-b' (INFERRED)
   15b. THE START, BOUNDED WHERE THE HELD SHEETS BOUND IT (the 502.3 ms of 12c withdrawn: 0.5 A is an input ceiling, not a delivered current)
     the input limits (MAKER, p.38): under 2.4 V of VSYS (VSYS_UVLO; rising 2.3/2.5/2.65 V, p.13) the input is clamped to 0.5 A, at most 10.48 W from VBUS20's
       20.96 V top; the sheet prints no minimum delivered current below that voltage (MAKER)
     the loads below 2.65 V: the converters on VSYS held off by their enables or their UVLOs (the LM5176 stages by logic, U12 on board E under
       its 3.8 V start, the heater buck by its divider); the resistors on VBAT (R2 100 k, R92 143 k, R96 143 k): at most 0.0636 mA at 2.65 V; the ICs' currents under UVLO are not
       all held (NETLIST, INFERRED); the energy to bring VSYS's 489 uF to 2.65 V: 1.717 mJ (INFERRED)
     the retries (MAKER): each failed start shuts the converter for 500 ms and retries for 10 ms; the 7th failure inside 90 s latches it, at
       most 3.062 s after the first window (INFERRED); with no pack only a POR clears it (VBUS re-plugged: "5 ms after either VBUS or VBAT becomes
       valid, the charger resets all the registers", p.27), with a pack the host does (it runs on the pack through the battery FET) (MAKER)
     so on held evidence the start ends in VSYS_MIN or in a latch within 3.062 s, never undefined; whether the first window succeeds is not
       bounded (no minimum delivered current): BENCH E11-31, acceptance: from cold, at VBUS20 19.15 and 20.96 V, with VSYS's maximum capacitance and the
