17. THE SECOND REVIEW (L4-CP01 TO L4-CP03, of the 22:30 checkpoint) AND THE EVIDENCE SPECIMENS
   17a. L4-CP01: U42'S FAULT ENVELOPE BY CASE (G = printed limit, I = inferred, T = typical only; SLVSET9G pp.7 to 10, 20 to 22, 26, 30, 31)
     the setting: I(OL) 1.4713 to 1.8018 A at R(ILIM) 11 kOhm (I: between the printed 9 and 30 kOhm rows, each G over TJ -40 to 125 C at VIN - VOUT
       1 V); a regulated, steady setting, NOT an instantaneous ceiling; the fast-trip threshold 2 x I(OL) and I(SCP) 45 A are T only (MAKER)
     (1) operating overload, I(OL) < I < I(FASTTRIP): held at the setting once the loop settles (the settling's peak is not printed); limiting for
       at most 202 ms (G), then off 500 to 800 ms (G) and a retry; a duty of at most 0.288; the contact at most 1.802 A steady, 15.9 K by w3de's rise (I)
     (2) a short applied while on: the current rises from VSYS's local capacitance (C236 and C23 to C25, the source's impedance behind them)
       until the fast trip; turn-off 2.2 to 4.5 us under I(SCP) (G, from a threshold that is T), about 1 us over it (T); then the device turns back
       on slowly into case (1) (p.21). A resistive EXTRAPOLATION, not a bound (I): 566 A would flow if VSYS's 17.375 V stood over RON's printed
       least 19 mOhm and the path's 11.7 mOhm with the contact at 0 and no inductance; TI prints RON at 0.6 to 6 A only (p.9), not at hundreds of
       amperes, so the FET's resistance there, its saturation and the loop's inductance are not printed: 566 A for 4.5 us (1.441 A2s) is E11-38's TEST
       TARGET for the recorded peak, and a reading over it revises the figure; the 813 prints no pulse rating, so the contact, the 24 AWG and the
       clamp are left to the bench's qualification (E11-38), not bounded (MAKER, INFERRED)
     the pins: IN at most 41.1 V by TI's Equation 14 at that extrapolation with U42 within 20 nH of C236 (90.7 uF effective, ESR 27 mOhm printed) against
       the absolute 67 V (I; the 20 nH a layout requirement, SESSION); OUT's negative spike through the output loop's inductance clamped by a
       Schottky D23 at OUT (TI 9.4.1, 9.5.1); OUT's -0.3 V absolute minimum is not shown under a clamp at hundreds of amperes: left to the bench (E11-38,
       Q-TI-18) (MAKER, INFERRED)
     (3) a start into a pre-existing short: limited at I(OL) from the start until the junction reaches T(J_REG) 136 to 154 C (G), then regulated
       to a lower current for the TIMEOUT t(Treg_timeout) 1.1 to 1.5 s (G), then off (p.22). The timeout starts when regulation begins; the time
       to reach it (VIN x I(OL) into the package from the air) and the regulated current are NOT PRINTED, so the TOTAL duration and the energy
       into the contact are not bounded by printed data; the setting's row is printed at VIN - VOUT 1 V, not at the 17.4 V a short puts across U42:
       the current at that bias, the pre-regulation interval and the regulated current are E11-38's (d) (MAKER, INFERRED)
     (4) repeated retry into a persistent short: each cycle is case (3), off at least 500 ms (G) between; the cycle's on-time is not bounded (3),
       so no duty is claimed (the 0.75 of the first version, from the timeout alone, is WITHDRAWN); what is bounded: after the first microseconds the
       current never exceeds the setting, so at any duty the contact's heating is at most case (1)'s 15.9 K by w3de's rise (I); an intermittent
       short applied and removed faster than the retry, and the recovery between, are not bounded by the device's timers: E11-38's (h) (INFERRED)
     the fans' start, against U42's least limit 1.471 A with U12's 0.8 A: both together at most 0.3356 A each, one at a time at most 0.5713 A (one other
       running at 0.1 A); VSYS_E at that current at least 9.494 V at the supplement floor: the fans must start at or under it (E11-35, E11-39) (INFERRED)
     the hotter interval: the current U42 regulates while at T(J_REG) is NOT PRINTED (under the setting, how far unknown): E11-38's (d) (MAKER)
     STATUS: sustained-overload remedy drafted; fault qualification open (E11-38: histories a to h, the pin excursions, the wiring's and copper's
       integrity, the contact body at or under 85 C); not evidence of a failure (SESSION)
   17b. L4-CP02: THE WHOLE HOT DOCKING WAVEFORM (a junction temperature does not extend ISM's printed 10 us at Tmb 25 C)
     the waveform to accept: 242.9 A peak, time constant 33.8 us, over IS's 80 A for 37.6 us, from a +70 C mounting base, once per docking event
     (D1) Nexperia's written acceptance of that waveform (Q-NXP-1, drafted, not sent): no circuit change; outside this project's control
     (D2) a defined pulse qualification on parts: 267.2 A peak and 37.2 us (x1.1), mounting base 75 C, 2000 pulses 10 s apart on each of 6 parts
       (over IS for 44.9 us); no circuit change; within its stated scope (a sample, not a production limit) (SESSION)
