       pulse and the hold, 154.6 ms to spare; from VIN_RAW passing U34's threshold to the restart's end at most 1.149 s (the pulse 201.2 ms, the hold
       0.907 s, the start 40.7 ms), longer while C-1c holds a hot pad (its cooling time NOT HELD, record l9stk's E-15)
     the UVLO edge (RECORD, l9stk): read at the falling edge, an input arriving within 34.0 ms of a latch does not restart the breaker; that
       fails safe (the breaker stays off, the hardware inhibit below holds the charge); the input's next return or a redocking restarts it
     THE HARDWARE CHARGE INHIBIT (SESSION, the same draft; the checker's B-R2: a persistent fault latches the -1 again with the input still
       present and no second pulse comes): Q47 (gate SYS_INH_G, DOCK_EN_OUT over R109 1M and R144 1M) turns Q49 (AO3401A) on through R82
       100k and R83 200k; Q49 holds CH_BATDRV at VBAT, so Q39, Q40 and Q42 are off and their body diodes point from the pack to VSYS: no
       charge leaves VSYS for the pack; Q48 (gate DD7_ALIVE) releases it once CELL+ is over 5.05 V. The signal: the loop powered (DOCK_EN_OUT
       alive: the pack's cells reach board P's breaker) and the terminal dead (CELL+ under 1.98 V): exactly the breaker off (latched, in its
       hold or starting) with the cells present; no firmware (MAKER, INFERRED)
     its levels (INFERRED): DOCK_EN_OUT at least 7.735 V docked (the pack's 10.6 V, RT1 at its cold least 5 kOhm, l8p's 10 k and 22 k), SYS_INH_G at
       least 3.829 V over Q47's 2.5 V threshold maximum; Q49's VGS -4.07 V at VSYS_MIN's 12.054 V (threshold -1.3 V at most) and -9.86 V at the 29.2 V
       clamp (12 V absolute); BATDRV meanwhile sinks at most 3.83 mA (11.5 V over its 3 kOhm least RBATDRV_ON, SLUSE65A; MAKER, INFERRED)
     the loop's load (INFERRED, an interface effect for records l9stk and l8p): the 2 MOhm sense at DOCK_EN_OUT moves the first inverter's gate
       at l9stk's bound point (10.6 V, RT1 at 47 kOhm) from 2.952 V to 2.939 V, against its 2.5 V threshold
     not inhibited, by design: with the loop unpowered (the gauge's FETs off, a pack absent, undocked) a pack's wake and precharge pass the
       breaker's body diodes at the gauge's own current (record l9stk's charge direction); source-only operation (U-04) is untouched (RECORD)
     E-14, EXTENDED TO A SECOND LATCH WITH THE INPUT PRESENT (INFERRED): with the inhibit the charge into a latched breaker is the battery
       FETs' off leakage (IDSS 1 uA at 25 C each, the hot value not printed); without it, at the breaker FET's VSD 1 V at most and IF-2's 52.5 C/W:
         the charger's ChargeCurrent at POR (TI's E2E answer, D4), 0.256 A: 0.256 W, TJ 89.7 C held
         R-b's largest actual current, 0x0200 inside TI's row condition, 1.2567 A: 1.257 W, TJ 142.2 C held
       so the inhibit is what holds a commanded charge beyond R-b off the FET (the checker's 4 A, 4 W, 276 C) wherever it sets (its reach
       below); E11-45 measures it (INFERRED)
     the charger-side hold (SESSION): hardware, the inhibit above, until the terminal is alive where it sets; the firmware's IF-7 reports the trip and writes
       ChargeCurrent only after the restart (E11-44); the hold does not wait on it
     ITS REACH, READ AFTER DRAFTING (INFERRED; the one design-out attempt): the inhibit sets only when CELL+ falls under 1.98 V. A latch while
       a source is present (the pack supplementing into the fault, the battery FETs on) leaves CELL+ tied to VSYS, which the charger holds
       into a resistive fault at sqrt(P x R): 10.4 V at the breaker's least-limit fault of 0.915 ohm with the front end's 118 W (its 5.7 A ISNS maximum)
       so the inhibit sets only for faults under 33 mOhm; when such a fault clears with the -1 latched, a charge passes the breaker's body
       diode with CELL+ reading alive. The breaker's PGD reads high in that state too (its VDS negative; LM5069 8.3.6 switches on VDS alone),
       so no board A signal tells a latched -1 passing charge from an -1 that is on: that case needs board P's gate state or a reverse-blocking
       element (route R1, board P's generator with record l9stk), or a hardware cap on the charge current on board A (route R2: above R-b's
       1.2567 A and under 1.405 A, the latched FET's body diode at 150 C held from 76.25 C at VSD 1 V and 52.5 C/W; a high-side current-sense part with
       a timed off-state, none held). Until one is drawn, a charge past R-b in that state rests on the firmware (R-b and IF-7); at R-b's
       largest the FET reads the E-14 row above (SESSION: R1 preferred; R2 the fallback)
     residuals (INFERRED): Q49 shorted holds the battery FETs off (their body diodes carry the discharge, and record l8p's PTC trips the breaker
       before their junctions pass 150 C); Q47, Q48 or Q49 open loses the inhibit or never releases it (both found by E11-45); a Q46 open lets
       an input's arrival drop a live pack for the pulse and the restart (E11-45 b); Q44 shorted holds the breaker off (fail-safe, revealed)
     STATUS: DD-7 DRAFTED for the first restart and for every latch whose fault takes CELL+ dead (the dark kit, a hard short, the input's
