   22d. THE STATES IN WHICH U47'S RESET SINKS, FROM THE DRAFT'S NETLIST (INFERRED from the netlist; TI's limits MAKER)
     DD7_N is pulled low by U47's RESET1 and RESET2 alone. Into it, while the loop reads powered (Q47, Q48 and Q52 on): R256 from CELL+ (Q48),
       R107 with R108 from CELL+ (Q52), R82 with R83 from VBAT (Q47), R254 and R255 from DD7_VC; with the loop unpowered only R255 (12.7 uA)
     the battery FETs Q39, Q40 and Q42 have their source on VBAT and their drain on CH_BATQ (check_dd7_netlist.py's BODY group reads it; a
       reversed FET reads FAIL): a P-channel FET's body diode conducts from drain to source, here from CELL+ towards VBAT, so once the inhibit
       holds their gates at VBAT nothing on VBAT can lift CELL+; it only bleeds, or is driven by the pack through the breaker
     state 1, the instant of setting: the FETs were on, a charge passing the off breaker's body diodes into the cells; CELL+ is at most VBAT,
       regulated to VSYS's 17.375 V (and held within the breaker FETs' VSD of the cells, 17.8 V at most): 3.85 mA, falling with the bleed
     state 2, the breaker restarted while the hold runs (5.82 s at most): CELL+ at the pack's 16.8 V at most: 3.72 mA
     state 3, a charger regulating high: CELL+ following VBAT up to SYSOVP's 19.5 V (SLUSE65A, the 4S row): 4.32 mA, still under 5 mA
     the states over 5 mA need CELL+ over 22.51 V, 3.01 V over SYSOVP: (i) a surge: VBAT at the SMCJ18A's 29.2 V clamp at the very instant of a set,
       with CELL+ lifted 4.71 V over the cells and their body-diode drop while the charge that set it flows: at most 6.45 mA, under the
       absolute 10 mA, and over 5 mA for at most 0.155 s of the bleed (a surge coinciding with the set: a second condition, V1's 'transient
       only'), or board P's BRK_VIN at its own 29.2 V clamp with the breaker restarted while a hold runs (the same bound, the pack pulling
       CELL+ back at once); (ii) sustained: a battery FET failed short AND VBAT held over
       22.51 V, which SYSOVP stops: two faults. At 6.45 mA VOL on the 60 ohm reading is about 0.39 V: the inhibit still holds (Q49's VGS under -9 V)
   22e. THE SELECTION (SESSION) AND WHAT IT COSTS
     no correction holds need 1 on printed figures alone: the breaker pair's hot leakage has no printed row, so each depends on record l8p's
       L8P-F06 (E-14c). (a) fails need 1 at the hot bound and at the air; (c) holds it by 0.396 s with a pair allowance of 451.2 uA, at the cost of
       a new part, an arm that reaches 0.91 of the way and a hold of up to 12.8 s; (b) holds it by 0.123 s with a pair allowance of 473.9 uA and the
       larger static room (0.846 mA against 0.597 mA), with no part beyond round 10's checked circuit
     SELECTED: (b), R256 back to 4.7 kOhm: at the hold as drawn it has the widest allowance for the unprinted leakage, and the higher
       ceiling if the hold is ever lengthened; (c) buys 36.9 uA more only with a hold of up to 19 s, about 1.1 K of case temperature on an
       assumed rate, which does not remove the dependence on E-14c; need 2 holds on TI's printed rows in every state without a second
       fault. It costs: U47's RESET over TI's recommended 5 mA in the named states of 22d
       (never over the absolute 10 mA), where 6.8 kOhm kept it under 5 mA in every state; and a margin of 0.123 s on an ASSUMED leakage
     reversed by: E-14c reading the breaker pair over 473.9 uA at its held case, or E11-45 (f2) reading the bleed outside the unit's hold; the next
       lever is then the hold on top of 4.7 kOhm (the static 0.846 mA is its ceiling), a new round with both checks' arithmetic beside it
   22f. V1'S AND V2'S ARITHMETIC SIDE BY SIDE (R256 has moved twice: 4.7 kOhm in round 10, 6.8 kOhm on V1's minor in round 11, 4.7 kOhm now; INFERRED)
     V1 (round 10's check, the sink at the clamp): 4.7 kOhm 6.39 mA, over TI's recommended 5 mA, 'transient only'; 6.8 kOhm 4.47 mA
     V2 (round 11's check, the bleed with the sources): 4.7 kOhm ends inside the hold for sources under 520.7 uA (1.218 s at the hot bound); 6.8 kOhm
